    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0098" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3065</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-26T11:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 26, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 28, 6.50
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3016. For Red Cross:</p>
                <p>Am forwarding report of Spanish inspectors dated November 1<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d22-f1"/> on camp at Brandenburg, containing 28 American prisoners
                    of whom 19 distributed in working camps, stating that treatment and discipline
                    good but— <pb facs="0099" n="15" xml:id="pg15"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Barracks, especially regarding heating, lighting and exposure to rain,
                            unsatisfactory;</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>That petty officers Kline and Roop compelled to work;</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Dr. John W. Brown, medical officer of <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Esmeraldas</hi>, detained contrary to Geneva convention.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Spanish Embassy has taken up these three points with Foreign Office. Food served
                    unsatisfactory but prisoners are receiving packages regularly and appear not
                    suffering in health or otherwise. Inspectors not allowed to converse without
                    witness. I suggest that you secure, if possible, confirmation of Doctor Brown’s
                    medical status. Dresel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
